{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/106922-after-reading-the-trinity-storyteller-s-handbook","id":106922,"title":"After reading the Trinity Storyteller's Handbook...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-06T08:44:32-07:00","id":106922,"title":"After reading the Trinity Storyteller's Handbook...","content":"I was completely blown away by it and thought that the game needed this book to turn a few things on it's head and to also add a bit more twists and uniqueness to things overall. I loved the information about alternate versions of Trinity. I really dug the story of Max Mercer. But what really got me was the new Modes. Has anyone done any work on them?<br /> Egomorphing, Precognition, Magnetokinesis, Entropokinesis, Probabilistics, Mindseive, Chronoportation and Iatrogenesis all sound awesome. Some of them have some rudimentary rules to them but I was wondering if anyone has tried to expand on them yet? If so, I would be interested in reading it. I have a thing for adding in new elements to tweak a setting some more and make it different from stock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T11:04:14-07:00","id":106986,"title":"","content":"Glad you liked it! I was happy with what we managed to accomplish, and always disappointed that we were never able to finish, but ... well, I got handed the reins to redo the entire setting. This is better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T01:15:33-07:00","id":107324,"title":"","content":"I understand it is superior. Vastly, so. Yes, I will be throwing all the money I have at any Trinity kickstarters. When the rules are released to the forums (I believe that was said), I will be playtesting them with my group. <br /> What intrigued me about the Aeoniverse was how every book evolved the setting in a much more concrete way than the other WW gaming lines. Each book gave me new things to tweak and adjust to the setting and allowed me to throw twists and turns to the players.<br /> My current group is more into Exalted than they are Aeoniverse, but I will change them. They played some Aberrant and some Adventure but both of those were alternate settings. Also, the ST is the only one who read the books and even then, he only read the crunch. This gives me the unique opportunity to throw things at them that they will not know.<br /> Overall, I wish that those powers had been expounded upon for more antagonists or NPC's that the players would be hard pressed to figure them out. Not to mention the whole thing with Mercer and the Venezuelan Phenomenon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}